{
  "title": "Normal random numbers (Box–Muller)",
  "function": "random_normals",
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "seed",
      "type": "int"
    },
    {
      "name": "n",
      "type": "int"
    }
  ],
  "returns": "vec",
  "library": true,
  "hints": [
    "Each pair of uniforms (u₁, u₂) becomes two normals: r = √(−2 ln u₁), θ = 2π u₂, then r·cos θ and r·sin θ.",
    "Generate 2·⌈n/2⌉ uniforms in one call to `random_uniforms(seed, …)`, use them in consecutive pairs (u[0], u[1]), (u[2], u[3]), …, and drop the last normal if n is odd.",
    "Your `random_uniforms` already validates the seed, and never returns exactly 0, so ln u₁ is always finite."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        2463534242,
        4
      ],
      "description": "two Box–Muller pairs",
      "expected": [
        -1.6455093556075222,
        -0.924431987362357,
        -1.185461226979586,
        0.24522960848372194
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        42,
        3
      ],
      "description": "an odd count: generate two pairs, keep three numbers",
      "expected": [
        -1.8404491768878464,
        -2.9126882475996063,
        1.2259084896854708
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        12345,
        6
      ],
      "description": "three pairs",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": [
        -0.5618647421287533,
        0.434851293980376,
        -0.8826335880605546,
        0.25465156476854794,
        0.17235003228156404,
        -1.8829258720864717
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        42,
        0
      ],
      "description": "zero numbers",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": []
    },
    {
      "args": [
        0,
        2
      ],
      "description": "seed 0 must still be rejected",
      "expect_error": true,
      "hidden": true
    }
  ]
}
